        <mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b&gt;Request flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Users talk to an agent running on AgentCore Runtime.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The agent calls tools through AgentCore Gateway with a reason and precheck session metadata.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Gateway forwards MCP calls to the precheck proxy (MCP target, untested). Deterministic rules run in-process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Rules that still need judgment send only their state_template fields to Jev through the NAT gateway.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Allowed calls reach your tools and results are checked on return. Denied calls get an error; escalated calls get an escalation ID.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The proxy pulls live policy (fails closed until first load) and reports decision events and escalations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Reviewers reach the web UI over Client VPN to approve escalations and publish rules. No built-in auth in the MVP.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;8&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The translator calls the Anthropic API to draft rules from plain language." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontColor=#232F3E;spacing=12;strokeColor=#AAB7B8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1530" y="430" width="300" height="510" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>